nts, output quality, and manifest\nconsistency. If any selected module or production entry lacks accepted detailed\nevidence, create exactly one successor `GD####` dispatcher for the next bounded\nwave. When all required evidence is accepted, create a final `GQ####` audit.\nOnly that audit may update the canonical bible/inventory and set manifest\n`status: accepted`, accepted `final_audit`, accepted module entries with output\npaths/GAME IDs/GPI IDs, and empty pending/blocked arrays after running the\ndedicated manifest completion check. The implementation-coverage validator is\nexplicitly deferred until F012. Do not create B or R files.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `GB0001.md`: only `G0001.md` and `G0002.md` for quiz content/editorial integrity.\n- `GB0002.md`: only `G0003.md` and `G0004.md` for round/score/progress rules.\n- `GB0003.md`: only `G0005.md` for accessible recovery and target parity.\n- `GC0001.md`: validates this wave and conditionally creates exactly one next `GD` or `GQ` file.\n- `../planning/game-design-manifest.json`: remains pending; this dispatcher records planned ownership only.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The generated G collection is bounded, batch-owned, and covers every selected module and GPI entry without expanding rejected/decision-gated scope.\n- `GC0001` and later GD/GQ work provide the required validation, dispatch, and final-audit loop.\n- The manifest cannot become accepted until durable G evidence, complete module/GAME/GPI coverage, and the dedicated completion check all pass.\n{\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"final_audit\": null,\n  \"pending_modules\": [\"quiz-content-and-editorial-integrity\", \"round-score-and-progress-rules\", \"accessible-recoverable-multitarget-experience\"],\n  \"blocked_modules\": [],\n  \"modules\": [\n    {\"module\":\"quiz-content-and-editorial-integrity\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"design_output_paths\":[\"game-design-runbooks/G0001.md\",\"game-design-runbooks/G0002.md\"],\"game_design_ids\":[\"GAME-001\"